## Review log

One row per pass. A section is not finished when it is written; it is finished when the rounds
stop producing changes.

| Round | Reviewer / lens | Date | Verdict | What changed |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| R1 | panel red-team (evaluator / legal / finance / delivery) | <date> | <pass/revise/blocked> | <what it caught> |

**Append, never overwrite, and only for rounds that ran.** A round that sends the section back and
is then re-run is two rows — `R1` then `R1 (2nd pass)`. Do not plant rows for R2 and R3 before they
happen: an empty row is not history, it puts later entries out of order, and the rounds still owed
are named below.

**Rounds are not a formality.** R1 catches whether it scores; R2 catches what only experience
sees — a claim that will not survive a client conversation, a promise the delivery team cannot
staff, a tone that reads wrong for this buyer. Do not collapse them.
